      "bullets": [
        "Firmware reverse-engineering of the TP-Link TL-841N router enables hardware-level access and root shell exploitation via local debug interfaces.",
        "Static binary analysis revealed hardcoded backdoor credentials stored directly within the router's embedded Linux image file system.",
        "Discovered backdoor credentials persist across standard factory resets because they reside in non-volatile, read-only flash partitions."
      ]
